{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-17470","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15833","text":"[&] Protocol — Agent Skills"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17472","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15834","marks":["bold"],"text":"Purpose:"},{"id":"spn-15835","text":" Teach any LLM or developer how to use the [&] Protocol correctly, idiomatically, and in the right sequence. These files cover everything from writing your first agent declaration to building providers that satisfy capability contracts."}]}],"id":"blk-17471","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-17473","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15836","text":"Quick Orientation"}]},{"id":"blk-17474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15837","text":"The [&] Protocol is a "},{"id":"spn-15838","marks":["bold"],"text":"language-agnostic specification for capability composition in AI agents"},{"id":"spn-15839","text":". It defines how agents declare cognitive capabilities ("},{"id":"spn-15840","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-15841","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15842","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-15843","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15844","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-15845","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15846","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-15847","text":"), how those compose via "},{"id":"spn-15848","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-15849","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-15850","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-15851","text":" operators, and how declarations compile into MCP and A2A configurations."}]},{"id":"blk-17475","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15852","text":"[&] sits at the "},{"id":"spn-15853","marks":["bold"],"text":"composition layer"},{"id":"spn-15854","text":" of the agent protocol stack — above MCP (agent-to-tool) and A2A (agent-to-agent). It does not replace either protocol. It generates configurations for both."}]},{"id":"blk-17476","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15855","text":"The Core Workflow"}]},{"id":"blk-17477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15856","text":"Every interaction with [&] follows this rhythm:"}]},{"id":"blk-17478","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. DECLARE   → Write an ampersand.json agent declaration\n2. VALIDATE  → Check it against the JSON Schema (draft 2020-12)\n3. COMPOSE   → Verify capability compatibility and ACI properties\n4. GENERATE  → Compile to MCP config and/or A2A agent card"},{"id":"blk-17479","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15857","text":"Skill Files"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-17481","spans":[{"id":"spn-15858","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-17482","spans":[{"id":"spn-15859","text":"What It Teaches"}]}],"id":"blk-17480","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-17483","spans":[{"id":"spn-15860","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/skills/01_DECLARATION.md"}],"text":"01_DECLARATION.md"}]},{"id":"blk-17484","spans":[{"id":"spn-15861","text":"Writing ampersand.json declarations — structure, capabilities, providers, config"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17485","spans":[{"id":"spn-15862","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/skills/02_VALIDATION.md"}],"text":"02_VALIDATION.md"}]},{"id":"blk-17486","spans":[{"id":"spn-15863","text":"Schema validation via CLI and SDKs — running checks, reading errors, batch mode"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17487","spans":[{"id":"spn-15864","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/skills/03_COMPOSITION.md"}],"text":"03_COMPOSITION.md"}]},{"id":"blk-17488","spans":[{"id":"spn-15865","text":"Capability composition — "},{"id":"spn-15866","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-15867","text":" operator, `\\"}]},{"id":"blk-17489","spans":[{"id":"spn-15868","text":">` pipelines, ACI properties, type safety"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17490","spans":[{"id":"spn-15869","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/skills/04_CONTRACTS.md"}],"text":"04_CONTRACTS.md"}]},{"id":"blk-17491",